# ============================================================
# GRADRIGHT — CURSOR AI MASTER RULES
# Primary client: Expo (React Native) in gradright-mobile/
# Backend: Python FastAPI in gradright-backend/ — ALL business logic here
# Optional: gradright-web/ (Next.js) for web-only surfaces — no business logic in Next API routes;
#   prefer calling FastAPI from the web app when extending the web client.
# ============================================================

## ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
- **Mobile (primary):** Expo / React Native (`gradright-mobile/`). TypeScript is the default for Expo; use project conventions.
- **Backend:** Python FastAPI — single source of business logic, AI (Claude), heavy DB work, OCR, PDF, email.
- **Database:** Supabase (PostgreSQL) via supabase-py + SQLAlchemy (async) in the backend.
- **AI:** Anthropic Python SDK (Claude); prompts live under `app/prompts/` in the backend.
- **Communication:** Expo app calls FastAPI over HTTPS (REST). FastAPI returns JSON (and SSE for streaming chat).
- **CORS:** FastAPI `CORSMiddleware` must allow the Expo dev origins (e.g. `http://localhost:8081`) and production app origins / schemes as configured.

## RELATED DOCS
- Backend build prompts: `PYTHON_BUILD_ORDER.md`
- Backend setup: `PYTHON_SETUP.md`
- Architecture reference: `ARCHITECTURE.md` (Expo SDK baseline noted there; verify when upgrading Expo)
- `BUILD_ORDER.md` describes an alternate **Next.js + Drizzle** path — do **not** treat it as the primary stack unless explicitly migrating; default new work to **Expo + FastAPI**.

---

## ABSOLUTE RULES — NEVER VIOLATE

### 1. LANGUAGE
- ALL backend code: **Python 3.11+** ONLY
- NO TypeScript, NO JavaScript in `gradright-backend/`
- NO Next.js, NO Node.js runtime inside the Python backend
- **Mobile:** TypeScript/JavaScript only inside `gradright-mobile/` — no Python there
- **Optional web (`gradright-web/`):** TypeScript/React per that project; keep domain logic in FastAPI

### 2. PYTHON STANDARDS
- Python version: 3.11+
- Package manager: pip with `requirements.txt`
- Virtual environment: always use venv (`python -m venv venv`)
- All Python files: type hints via `typing` / modern builtins
- All Python functions: docstrings
- Line length: max 100 characters
- Formatting: Black-compatible (4-space indent, no trailing whitespace)

### 3. FRAMEWORK + LIBRARIES (backend)
- Web framework: FastAPI ONLY
- HTTP server: Uvicorn
- Database ORM: SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async) + Alembic
- Supabase client: supabase-py (auth + storage)
- Validation: Pydantic v2 for ALL request/response models
- AI: anthropic (official Python SDK)
- OCR: pytesseract (dev) → boto3 Textract (production)
- Email: resend
- HTTP client (outbound): httpx (async)
- Rate limiting: slowapi
- Redis: redis-py (async)
- PDF: reportlab
- Environment: python-dotenv + pydantic-settings
- CORS: `fastapi.middleware.cors.CORSMiddleware`

### 4. FOLDER STRUCTURE — gradright-backend/ (target layout)
```
gradright-backend/
├── main.py
├── requirements.txt
├── .env                 # Never commit
├── .env.example
├── alembic.ini
├── alembic/
│   └── versions/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── config.py
│   ├── database.py
│   ├── supabase_client.py
│   ├── models/
│   ├── schemas/
│   ├── routers/
│   ├── services/
│   ├── prompts/
│   ├── data/
│   ├── utils/
│   └── middleware/
├── tests/
└── scripts/
```

### 5. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (exact names)
See `gradright-backend/.env.example`. Required for full features; health-only local runs may use placeholders until Supabase/DB are connected.

### 6. API RESPONSE FORMAT
Use `APIResponse[T]` from `app/schemas/base.py` for JSON endpoints (see existing rule examples in this file historically).

### 7. DATABASE RULES
- Async SQLAlchemy 2.0; UUID `id`, `created_at`, `updated_at` on tables
- Migrations via Alembic only (once DB layer is active)

### 8. ERROR HANDLING RULES
- try/except in route handlers; `HTTPException` for expected errors; log with `logging.error`; no stack traces to clients in production
- Log format: `[ROUTER][FUNCTION] Error description: {error}`

### 9. AUTHENTICATION RULES
- Supabase Auth; `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from the Expo app
- `get_current_user` in `app/middleware/auth.py`; NBFC routes require `nbfc_supervisor`

### 10. STREAMING (chatbot)
- `StreamingResponse` + Claude `messages.stream()`; SSE chunks `data: {text}\n\n`

---

## SERVICE LAYER RULES
- Thin routers; logic in `app/services/`
- No Claude calls from routers — use `claude_service.py`

## WHAT CURSOR MUST NEVER DO
- Put business logic in route handlers (backend)
- Call Anthropic from routers directly
- Hardcode secrets
- Use sync DB calls in FastAPI
- Skip Pydantic validation on route bodies
- Return untyped `dict` from public APIs — use Pydantic schemas
- Add Python packages without updating `requirements.txt`
